# Project Rules - Next.js 14 + Supabase Refactoring

## Core Standards
- TypeScript strict mode - NO `any` types
- Server Components by default - Only use `'use client'` when absolutely necessary
- NO middleware - Use Layout Protection instead
- Homepage design (`src/app/page.tsx`) is the ONLY design reference
- NO mock data - 100% dynamic from Supabase/APIs
- ALL colors/fonts/spacing from homepage design system (`src/styles/centralized.css`)

## Structure Requirements

### Centralized Locations
- All queries: `lib/supabase/queries/`
- All validation: `lib/validations/` (Zod schemas)
- All constants: `lib/constants/` (routes, api-endpoints, messages, errors, config, permissions)
- All errors: `lib/errors/` (app-error.ts, error-handler.ts, error-codes.ts)
- All theme: `lib/theme/` (colors.ts, typography.ts, spacing.ts, shadows.ts, borders.ts, animations.ts)
- All utils: `lib/utils/`
- All hooks: `lib/hooks/`
- All services: `lib/services/`
- All config: `lib/config/`

## Authentication
- Layout Protection for pages (no middleware)
- `withAuth()` wrapper for Server Actions
- `withAPIAuth()` wrapper for API Routes
- Use `lib/auth/helpers.ts` for auth utilities

## Styling Rules
- ONLY use colors from homepage design system
- NO inline styles - use Tailwind classes or CSS variables
- Dark mode must work correctly
- Use `cn()` utility for class merging
- All colors must use CSS variables: `var(--brand-primary)`, `var(--text-primary)`, etc.

## Data Rules
- NO mock data - remove all mock/fake/dummy/sample/test data
- Server Components for data fetching
- Loading states required
- Error states required
- Empty states required
- All data from Supabase or external APIs

## Component Rules
- Server Components by default
- Client Components only for: interactivity, hooks, browser APIs
- Use shadcn/ui pattern with homepage design
- All forms must be centralized
- All shared components in `components/shared/`

## Validation
- All forms use Zod schemas from `lib/validations/`
- Error messages from `lib/constants/messages.ts`
- Validation happens in Server Actions, not client

## Error Handling
- Use `AppError` class from `lib/errors/app-error.ts`
- Use global error handler from `lib/errors/error-handler.ts`
- Error codes from `lib/errors/error-codes.ts`
- Log errors using `lib/utils/logger.ts`

## Performance
- Use React `cache()` for data fetching
- Server Components by default
- Dynamic imports for heavy components
- Next.js Image component for all images

## File Naming
- Components: PascalCase (e.g., `UserProfile.tsx`)
- Utilities: camelCase (e.g., `formatDate.ts`)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., `API_ENDPOINTS`)
- Types: PascalCase (e.g., `UserType`)

## Import Order
1. React/Next.js imports
2. Third-party imports
3. Internal imports (`@/...`)
4. Types
5. Constants

## Comments
- Use Arabic comments for business logic
- Use English comments for technical explanations
- Document all public functions
